---
/**
 * The data model reference.
 *
 * The body of this page is not written here. It is the `data-model` entry of the
 * generated `reference` collection, emitted by tools/codegen from
 * spec/mcpd.spec.json. This file supplies only the frame: what the document is,
 * why it is generated, and an index into it, since the document is long.
 *
 * The index is built from the rendered headings rather than kept by hand, so a
 * field added to the spec appears in it with nothing edited here.
 */
import Doc from '@/layouts/Doc.astro'
import SignalFlow from '@/components/SignalFlow.astro'
import { getEntry, render } from 'astro:content'
import spec from '@/generated/spec-index.json'

const entry = await getEntry('reference', 'data-model')
if (!entry) {
  throw new Error(
    'src/content/reference/data-model.md is missing. Run `make gen` to write it from spec/mcpd.spec.json.',
  )
}
const { Content, headings } = await render(entry)

/* The generated document has two second-level headings, Enumerations and
   Entities, and one third-level heading per named thing under them. Grouping
   the h3s under the h2 they follow reproduces the document's own structure. */
interface Group {
  title: string
  slug: string
  items: { text: string; slug: string }[]
}
const groups: Group[] = []
for (const h of headings) {
  if (h.depth === 2) groups.push({ title: h.text, slug: h.slug, items: [] })
  else if (h.depth === 3 && groups.length > 0) {
    groups[groups.length - 1]!.items.push({ text: h.text, slug: h.slug })
  }
}
---

<Doc
  title="Data model"
  description="Every entity, field and enumerated value mcpd stores, generated from spec/mcpd.spec.json so it cannot drift from the running server."
  lede="Every entity, field and enumerated value the daemon stores. Generated from the same specification the server, the OpenAPI document and all six SDKs are built from."
  og="docs"
>
  <div class="not-prose well max-w-[68ch] px-4 py-3.5">
    <p class="legend text-ink-3">Generated file</p>
    <p class="mt-1.5 max-w-[62ch] text-[0.875rem] leading-relaxed text-ink-2">
      Everything below this page's introduction is produced by
      <span class="data text-ink">tools/codegen</span> from
      <span class="data text-ink">spec/mcpd.spec.json</span>. Do not edit it by
      hand. Change the spec, run <span class="data text-ink">make gen</span>, and
      the server, the SDKs and this page all move together.
      <span class="data text-ink">make check</span> fails the build when any of them drift apart.
    </p>
  </div>

  <p>
    A hand-written reference describes the code as it was on the day somebody
    typed it out. This one is emitted from the specification the server's Rust
    types are compiled from, so a field can only appear here if it exists in the
    build you are running.
  </p>

  <h2>How to read it</h2>
  <p>
    There are {spec.counts.enums} enumerations and {spec.counts.types + spec.counts.entities}
    object shapes. The enumerations come first: closed sets of values, such as the
    {spec.counts.spanKinds} kinds a span can be, or the four values a span's status can
    take. Everything after them is an object.
  </p>
  <ul>
    <li>
      An object with a <strong>Stored in</strong> line is an entity: a record mcpd
      keeps, with the table it lives in, its primary key and its indexes.
    </li>
    <li>
      An object without one is a shape that travels in a request or a response, and
      is never stored under its own name.
    </li>
    <li>
      A field's type links to the type it names. A field marked
      <strong>required</strong> must be present; everything else may be omitted,
      and an omitted field is absent rather than empty.
    </li>
  </ul>

  <h2>Why one model, not six</h2>
  <p>
    Spans, logs, metrics, scores, feedback and aspect notes are stored
    separately, but every one of them carries the trace identifier of the run it
    belongs to, and most of them the span identifier of the step as well. That is
    the reason they are one model. Without those identifiers you have six
    separate stores: a log line nothing ties to the run that emitted it, a cost
    figure that leads back to no prompt, a low score with nothing to read
    underneath it, a sentence about a run you cannot open. Correlation is what
    makes the rest of this page worth having.
  </p>

  <SignalFlow class="not-prose my-8" />

  <h2>Index</h2>
  <p>The document is long. This is a jump table into it.</p>

  <nav class="not-prose reference-index panel my-6 overflow-hidden" aria-label="Data model contents">
    {
      groups.map((g) => (
        <div class="border-t border-scribe-2 first:border-t-0">
          <div class="flex items-baseline justify-between gap-4 bg-panel-1 px-4 py-2.5">
            <a href={`#${g.slug}`} class="legend text-ink transition-colors hover:text-amber">
              {g.title}
            </a>
            <span class="data text-[0.75rem] text-ink-3">{g.items.length}</span>
          </div>
          <ul class="grid gap-x-8 gap-y-1 bg-panel-2 px-4 py-4 sm:grid-cols-2 lg:grid-cols-4">
            {g.items.map((it) => (
              <li>
                <a
                  href={`#${it.slug}`}
                  class="data block truncate text-[0.8125rem] text-ink-2 transition-colors hover:text-amber"
                >
                  {it.text}
                </a>
              </li>
            ))}
          </ul>
        </div>
      ))
    }
    <p class="border-t border-scribe-2 bg-panel-1 px-4 py-2.5 text-[0.8125rem] text-ink-3">
      Specification <span class="data text-ink-2">{spec.specVersion}</span>, API
      <span class="data text-ink-2">{spec.apiVersion}</span>.
    </p>
  </nav>

  <div class="reference reference--model">
    <Content />
  </div>
</Doc>
